---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description={`Cookie Policy for ${SITE.name}. Information about how I use cookies and local storage.`}
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:py-20">

    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-red-500 transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">›</span>
      Cookie Policy
    </p>

    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mb-3">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm mb-10">Last updated: February 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-zinc-200 space-y-8">

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">What Are Cookies?</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Cookies are small text files that websites can store on your device. They are used
          for various purposes, including remembering your preferences, keeping you logged in,
          and tracking how visitors use a site.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-2">
          This page explains how <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> uses cookies and related technologies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Cookies I Use</h2>

        <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-xl px-5 py-4 mb-4">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-green-900 text-sm mb-2">Good news: I don't currently use tracking cookies</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-green-800 leading-relaxed">
            I do not use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, or any other third-party tracking service.
            I don't serve advertising cookies. I don't use session cookies for login purposes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display text-base font-bold text-white mb-2">Cookie Consent Preference (Local Storage)</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
          When you interact with the cookie notice at the bottom of my site, I save your preference
          (accepted or rejected) in your browser's <strong>localStorage</strong>. This is stored
          entirely within your own browser — no data is sent to my servers.
        </p>
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-zinc-950">
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 font-semibold text-zinc-200">Key</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 font-semibold text-zinc-200">Purpose</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 font-semibold text-zinc-200">Stored in</th>
              <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 font-semibold text-zinc-200">Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 font-mono text-xs">svl_cookie_consent</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800">Stores your accept/reject choice</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800">localStorage (your browser only)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800">Until you clear your browser data</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400">
          Note: localStorage is not technically a cookie — it does not get sent with HTTP requests
          and is only accessible by my website within your browser. Under UK GDPR guidance, similar
          storage technologies to cookies may require the same level of transparency.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Self-Hosted Fonts</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
          This site uses the <strong>Inter</strong> typeface, loaded from files hosted on my own
          web server (via Netlify's CDN). Unlike loading from Google Fonts, this does not send your
          IP address or any other data to Google's servers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-2">
          My website is hosted by <strong>Netlify, Inc.</strong> Netlify's servers receive standard
          web server log data (including your IP address) when you visit any page. This is standard
          behaviour for any hosted website and is covered by
          <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-500 hover:text-red-500">
            Netlify's Privacy Policy
          </a>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Form submissions via my quote request form are processed and stored by Netlify Forms.
          See my <a href="/privacy" class="text-red-500 hover:text-red-500">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">How to Manage or Delete Cookie Data</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-2">
          To remove the consent preference stored in localStorage, you can:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <li>Open your browser's developer tools (press F12)</li>
          <li>Go to the "Application" or "Storage" tab</li>
          <li>Select "Local Storage" and find my site</li>
          <li>Delete the <code class="bg-zinc-900 px-1 rounded text-xs font-mono">svl_cookie_consent</code> key</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3">
          Alternatively, clearing all site data from your browser settings will remove this preference.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-2">
          You can also find general cookie management guidance at:
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/your-data-matters/online/cookies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-500 hover:text-red-500">
            ico.org.uk/your-data-matters/online/cookies/
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
          If I add analytics or other cookies in future, I will update this policy and my cookie
          banner accordingly. Check the date at the top of this page to see when it was last updated.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Contact Me</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Questions about cookies or your privacy? Please contact me:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-red-500 hover:text-red-500">{SITE.email}</a></p>
          <p><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href={SITE.phone.href} class="text-red-500 hover:text-red-500">{SITE.phone.display}</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

    <!-- Back link -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-zinc-800">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-red-500 hover:text-red-500 transition-colors">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to home
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
